WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.957
Keep router output small and structured.

00:00:02.957 --> 00:00:10.257
A router might return three things: a route, a policy search query, and an order I D.

00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:13.396
That is enough to execute the next actions.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.798
The router does not need to write the final answer.

00:00:16.798 --> 00:00:22.948
It does not need to produce a paragraph of explanation.

00:00:22.948 --> 00:00:27.668
Its job is to transform a user request into machine-readable execution instructions.

00:00:27.668 --> 00:00:32.618
For example, route equals policy and order.

00:00:32.618 --> 00:00:35.303
Policy query equals return deadline after delivery.

00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:39.019
Order I D equals one zero four two.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:46.892
This separation improves testing. You can evaluate routing without also evaluating answer quality.

00:00:46.892 --> 00:00:52.916
If the wrong source is selected, you know the router failed before generation even begins.
